 ## Overview
-This method maps a 2D semantic label image to an RGB color image by assigning predefined colors to known classes and generating deterministic HSV-based colors for unknown or unseen classes [S1, unofficial]. It ensures visual consistency and distinctness for arbitrary label IDs without requiring user-defined palettes for every possible class [S1, unofficial]. It differs from [Categorical Color Maps](7160-categorical-color-maps.md) by using a deterministic hash-based hue generation for unknown labels rather than a fixed or random palette, and from [Style Transfer Function (1D)](777-style-transfer-function-1d.md) by operating on discrete integer labels rather than continuous scalar values [S1, Parent, unofficial].
+This method maps a 2D semantic label image to an RGB color image by assigning predefined colors to known classes and generating deterministic HSV-based colors for unknown or unseen classes [S1, unofficial]. It ensures visual consistency and distinctness for arbitrary label IDs without requiring user-defined palettes for every possible class [S1, unofficial]. It differs from [Categorical Color Maps](7160-categorical-color-maps.md) by using a deterministic hash-based hue generation for unknown labels rather than a fixed or random palette, and from [Style Transfer Function (1D)](777-style-transfer-function-1d.md) by operating on discrete integer labels rather than continuous scalar values [S1, unofficial].
 
